<article class="env-lemma" id="084N">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/084N">Lemma <span data-tag="084N">67.17.8</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $B$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $f, g : X \to Y$ be morphisms of algebraic spaces over $B$. Let $U \subset X$ be an open subspace such that $f|_ U = g|_ U$. If the scheme theoretic closure of $U$ in $X$ is $X$ and $Y \to B$ is separated, then $f = g$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      As $Y \to B$ is separated the fibre product $Y \times _{\Delta , Y \times _ B Y, (f, g)} X$ is a closed subspace $Z \subset X$. As $f|_ U = g|_ U$ we see that $U \subset Z$. Hence $Z = X$ as $U$ is assumed scheme theoretically dense in $X$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>